<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36616" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plaustrārĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plostr-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		plaustrum, plostrum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a
			wagon</i>, <i>wagon-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">asini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 11, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juga duo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plau-strārĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plostr-</span></b> ), ii,
				m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A wagon - maker</i>, <i>wheelwright</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plaustrariorum vectigal,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Alex. Sev. 24</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A wagon - driver</i>, <i>wagoner</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si Aquiliae actione plaustrarium (al.
					plostrarium) teneri placet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					9, 2, 27 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
